{"path":"ranges/chunk_by_view/begin","title":"std::ranges::chunk_by_view<V,Pred>::begin","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::chunk_by_view&lt;V,Pred&gt;::</span>begin","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view/begin","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Returns an iterator to the first element of the chunk_by_view.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns an <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view/iterator\">iterator</a> to the first element of the <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view\"><code>chunk_by_view</code></a>.\n</p><p>Equivalent to:\n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> iter<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>begin_.<span class=\"me1\">has_value</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    iter <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> begin_.<span class=\"me1\">value</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    iter <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*find_next*/</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    begin_ <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> iter<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// caching</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n<p>The behavior is undefined if the underlying predicate <code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view#pred\">pred_</a></i></code> does not contain a value.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view/iterator\">Iterator</a> to the first element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>In order to provide the amortized constant-time complexity required by the <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><code>range</code></a> concept, this function caches the result within the data member <code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view#begin\">begin_</a></i></code> for use on subsequent calls.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_by_view/end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>end</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::begin</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> returns an iterator to the beginning of a range<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/chunk_by_view","title":"std::ranges::views::chunk_by, std::ranges::chunk_by_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::chunk_by_view<V,Pred>::begin","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++23. Returns an iterator to the first element of the chunk_by_view."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Iterator to the first element."},{"label":"Notes","note":"In order to provide the amortized constant-time complexity required by the range concept, this function caches the result within the data member begin_ for…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"end","note":"returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end"},{"label":"ranges::begin","note":"returns an iterator to the beginning of a range"}]}]},"standards":["C++20","C++23"],"wordCount":125,"codeBlockCount":1}
